{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "purpose": "Evidence-backed Clockify service-routing matrix (ROUTE-001). H02-ROUTING-approved 2026-07-27; ROUTE-002 shipped runtime routing in SDK 0.13.0. No runtime code imports this file -- wrapper/internal/routing.ts keeps an equality-pinned hand-written copy of the approved rows, guarded by wrapper/tests/routing-matrix-equality.test.ts. Every non-null row carries a sourcePointer and proofKind; every unsupported combination is explicit (url: null + unsupportedReason).",
  "approved": true,
  "approvedBy": "apet97",
  "approvedDate": "2026-07-27",
  "sourceRevision": "092642d",
  "nonGoals": [
    "Live-confirming regional/US/UK/AU/developer profile routing against a real regional or subdomain-configured workspace is explicitly deferred: no such sacrificial workspace is currently available (confirmed 2026-07-27). These rows remain liveConfirmationRequired:true, shipped as opt-in if/when ROUTE-002 implements them -- never as globally-trusted defaults -- until a regional/subdomain sandbox becomes available.",
    "Removing pto.api.clockify.me / auditing developer.clockify.me in wrapper/internal/authenticated-boundary-fetch.ts and scripts/sdk-codegen/emitter.mjs's allowlists is runtime code (ROUTE-002), out of scope for this evidence-only matrix. This approval only records that pto.api.clockify.me is confirmed dead/speculative (see conflicts[0])."
  ],
  "sources": {
    "official": "spec/official/clockify.official.openapi.yaml#/info/description (\"## API URLs\" and \"## Regional Server Prefixes\" sections)",
    "corrected": "spec/corrected/clockify.corrected.openapi.yaml (root #/servers and per-operation #/paths/*/*/servers overrides)",
    "existingAllowlists": [
      "wrapper/internal/authenticated-boundary-fetch.ts (CLOCKIFY_PROD_HOSTS)",
      "scripts/sdk-codegen/emitter.mjs (CLOCKIFY_API_HOSTS)"
    ]
  },
  "operationServiceDerivation": {
    "method": "Every corrected-spec operation resolved by its effective server (operation-level `servers` override, else the first root `servers` entry), classified by hostname. Computed live by scripts/service-routing-matrix.mjs against spec/corrected/clockify.corrected.openapi.yaml; the checker compares these stored counts to the current derivation and fails closed on drift.",
    "totalOperations": 168,
    "counts": { "api": 157, "reports": 10, "audit": 1 },
    "note": "No operation resolves to a fourth host. \"pto\" (time-off) operations resolve to the regular api host -- there is no per-operation servers override routing them elsewhere. This is empirical fact, not evidence that time-off has no distinct service; see conflicts[0]."
  },
  "regionalPrefixes": {
    "euc1": "EU (Germany)",
    "use2": "USA",
    "euw2": "UK",
    "apse2": "AU"
  },
  "profiles": {
    "global": {
      "regular": {
        "url": "https://api.clockify.me/api/v1",
        "sourcePointer": "spec/corrected/clockify.corrected.openapi.yaml#/servers/0; spec/official#/info/description \"API URLs > Global > Regular\"",
        "proofKind": "spec-corrected+official-doc",
        "liveConfirmationRequired": false
      },
      "reports": {
        "url": "https://reports.api.clockify.me/v1",
        "sourcePointer": "spec/corrected/clockify.corrected.openapi.yaml#/servers/1 and 10 per-operation overrides; spec/official#/info/description \"API URLs > Global > Reports\"",
        "proofKind": "spec-corrected+official-doc",
        "liveConfirmationRequired": false
      },
      "audit": {
        "url": "https://auditlog-api.api.clockify.me/v1",
        "sourcePointer": "spec/corrected/clockify.corrected.openapi.yaml#/servers/2 and 1 per-operation override",
        "proofKind": "spec-corrected",
        "liveConfirmationRequired": false,
        "note": "Not documented in spec/official's prose (no audit host example there); proven directly by the corrected spec's own operation override instead."
      },
      "pto": {
        "url": null,
        "unsupportedReason": "Confirmed by H02-ROUTING (apet97, 2026-07-27): pto.api.clockify.me is dead/speculative allowlist code, not a real routed service -- see conflicts[0]. No corrected-spec operation resolves to a distinct pto host; time-off operations resolve to the regular api host (see operationServiceDerivation). This row intentionally does NOT default to the api host: that would assert pto has no distinct service by inference rather than by confirmed decision."
      }
    },
    "eu": {
